WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.130
Avengers: Infinity War might've pleased audiences
everywhere, but if you're a fan of the Incredible

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.910
Hulk, the film may have been a bit frustrating
to watch.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:08.910
Why?

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.690
Well, we might as well get this big, green,
spoiler out of the way right now:

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:16.219
In the beginning, the green giant withstands
a brutal beating by Thanos before being whisked

00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:20.900
away to Earth by Heimdall, and that's the
last time you see him in his full green glory.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.640
Bruce Banner tries and fails several times
to get his other half to come out and play,

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.510
but the Hulk refuses to emerge.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.720
So why is the Hulk being shy all of a sudden?

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.320
The most obvious answer is that he simply
doesn't want to endure a second round against

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.239
the Mad Titan, but there might be more to
it than just that.

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:39.609
Let's take a look at why the other guy doesn't
want to play the hero game anymore.

00:00:39.609 --> 00:00:40.819
Father of mine

00:00:40.819 --> 00:00:45.659
One regrettable aspect of Bruce Banner's portrayal
in the MCU is that, as popular as Banner's

00:00:45.659 --> 00:00:49.640
"I'm always angry" line from Avengers has
become, the movies have never explored exactly

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.499
why that rage is always with him.

00:00:51.499 --> 00:00:56.000
So, it's possible that directors Joe and Anthony
Russo are using Thanos to finally give us

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.440
a glimpse of that story.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:03.760
In the 1985 comic Incredible Hulk #312, longtime
Hulk writer Bill Mantlo wrote one of Bruce

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.590
Banner's most memorable and influential stories.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:09.000
Most of the tale is a flashback to Banner's
younger days.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.720
We learn that both Bruce and his mother Rebecca
endured extreme emotional and physical abuse

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:16.080
at the hands of Bruce's father, Brian Banner.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.570
Brian eventually ends his wife's life for
trying to escape from him.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:24.580
Mantlo essentially told readers that the gamma
bomb blast from 1962's Incredible Hulk #1

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:25.810
didn't create the Hulk.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:29.890
The trauma Bruce endured created the Hulk,
the gamma blast just set him free.

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.240
It's possible that what's stopping the Hulk
from emerging in Infinity War isn't that the

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:37.170
beating he took from Thanos scared him, but
that it reawakened his childhood trauma.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:41.640
In fact, this could be why a certain bizarre
scene was deleted from Thor: Ragnarok.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:46.000
In the scene, Banner expresses regret at missing
his father's death because he was too busy

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:46.620
working.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:50.840
"I missed my own father's death because I
was focusing on my destiny."

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.800
But that would be a strange thing to say,
since not only did the comic book Banner have

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:58.730
no fluffy feelings for his father, but it
was eventually revealed that Bruce Banner

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:00.370
actually killed his father.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:04.460
If the Infinity War filmmakers plan to use
Hulk's shyness as a way to introduce the abuse

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:08.649
backstory, the conversation from the deleted
scene wouldn't have made sense.

00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:11.060
A Hulk humiliated

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.950
Maybe the Hulk isn't scared and maybe the
Hulk isn't traumatized.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.090
Maybe he's just embarrassed.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:18.970
The Hulk has never experienced the kind of
defeat Thanos handed him in the opening of

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:19.970
Avengers: Infinity War.

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:23.870
And the Green Goliath doesn't just have the
intelligence of a toddler; he has the emotional

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.340
maturity of one too.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.750
The beating he took may have destroyed his
confidence.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.510
The Hulk doesn't have any particular skills
like his teammates.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.030
Instead the Hulk's sole purpose is to beat
people up.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:36.510
If he can't do that then, in his mind, how
could he be anything but worthless?

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:40.920
It's worth remembering that not only is Banner
around other Avengers each time he tries to

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:44.790
change into the Hulk in Infinity War, but
there's a specific Avenger he's being reminded

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.090
of, Tony Stark.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:49.790
Tony's the only guy other than Thanos who's
managed to knock the Hulk out.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:54.040
The first time Banner tries to change in Infinity
War, Tony's right there, urging him to Hulk

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.040
out.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.531
The second time, during the battle in Wakanda,
Tony's nowhere to be found, but Banner is

00:02:58.531 --> 00:03:03.060
inside the Hulkbuster armor...inside the suit
that not only gave the Hulk one of his only

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.400
defeats, but was created solely for the purpose
of beating up the Hulk.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.459
It's possible that it was the wrong time to
remind the Green Goliath of that.

00:03:10.459 --> 00:03:11.490
Third rock from the sun

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:15.849
But maybe the reason Hulk refuses to emerge
may not have anything at all to do with Thanos

00:03:15.849 --> 00:03:16.849
at all.

00:03:16.849 --> 00:03:18.330
Maybe it's the Earth that's the problem.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:22.520
Thor, Loki, Valkyrie, and even Banner may
have been fine with leaving Sakaar in Thor:

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.400
Ragnarok, but the Hulk didn't have much say
in the matter.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.260
During their first one-on-one dialogue scene
together, Hulk even told Thor plainly he had

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.230
no intention of returning to Earth.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:31.760
Why?

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:32.760
"Earth hate Hulk."

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.980
On Sakaar, Hulk was treated better than he'd
ever been.

00:03:35.989 --> 00:03:37.460
No one even knew about Banner.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:41.400
The people of Sakaar didn't run screaming
from him for smashing his enemies; they cheered

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.040
him.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.040
They had parades for him.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.400
Why would he want to leave?

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.870
So perhaps after he's sent to New York, Hulk
decides he just doesn't want to fight to protect

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.660
the place that seems to hate him so much.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:51.980
The blame game

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:54.520
We've already talked about the Hulk's fear
and humiliation.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.489
But it's also possible Hulk's refusal to fight
was about guilt,.and friendship.

00:03:58.489 --> 00:04:03.220
Right after the Hulk is defeated by Thanos,
Heimdall uses his last few breaths to transport

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:04.680
Hulk to Earth so he can warn them.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:08.310
That means the first time Banner tries to
Hulk out, as far as the Hulk knows, he's the

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:13.310
only survivor of the Asgardian refugee ship,
and that Thor, Valkyrie, and everyone else

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.310
is dead.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:18.060
Considering Thor and Hulk formed a bond during
Ragnarok, perhaps his belief that he wasn't

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.489
strong enough to save his friend would be
crushing.

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:24.500
If so, the revelation that Thor was really
alive during the Battle of Wakanda could be

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:28.880
a huge relief, and might help clear the way
for Hulk's arrival in Avengers 4.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:30.550
So he can do this again:

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:32.880
Thanks for watching!

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:35.600
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.810
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

